    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d656">

                <pb facs="0611" n="599" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg599"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/2299: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Egypt</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>)<anchor n="94" xml:id="d656-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-05T13:00:00-04:00">April 5, 1944—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>737. Your 750, March 29, 4 p.m. You may inform the Egyptian Prime Minister that
                    his message has been communicated to the President. You may wish to refer in
                    your reply to the assurances and observations contained in the Department’s 657
                    and 692<anchor n="95" xml:id="d656-f2"/> as well as other recent communications
                    on the subject.</p>
                <p>Repeat to Jidda, Baghdad, Jerusalem, Beirut and Damascus.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d656-f1" n="94" type="source" xml:id="d656-f1-content">
                <p>The substance of this telegram was approved by President Roosevelt.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d656-f2" n="95" xml:id="d656-f2-content">
